board Hot 100 at the top position. It was the last of Jackson's 13 solo career number ones and achieved its instant success due to Sony Music's \"magic trick\" of promoting it to radio for two months before its retail release, making it the seventh most played song at US radio by the time it hit stores and generating 120,000 first-week sales. However, it spent only one week at number one and is considered a \"second-tier\" hit, less fondly remembered by fans and receiving low airplay in 2025 compared to other Jackson hits, partly because it was written by R. Kelly. \"Michael Jackson's You Are Not Alone debuted at number one the first week of September 1995.\"","year":1995,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Hit Parade Music History and Music Trivia","episode":"Toppermost of the Poppermost Edition Part 1","url":"https://shows.acast.com/hit-parade/episodes/695d4ef60c30a1408dc29358"},{"source":"Hit Parade Music History and Music Trivia","episode":"Toppermost of the Poppermost Edition Part 1","url":null}]}],"book_tracks":[],"others":[{"id":187196401546005,"type":"album","name":"Thriller","year":1981,"weight":163},{"id":223498080057316,"type":"song","name":"Beat It","year":1983,"weight":59},{"id":20917270846242,"type":"song","name":"Billie Jean","year":1983,"weight":52},{"id":236040607690380,"type":"album","name":"Off the Wall","year":1979,"weight":41},{"id":100781197787300,"type":"album","name":"Bad","year":1987,"weight":34},{"id":48744200805795,"type":"song","name":"Thriller","year":1984,"weight":27},{"id":5852980504029,"type":"song","name":"Rock with You","year":1980,"weight":25},{"id":268164961577260,"type":"song","name":"Scream","year":1995,"weight":22},{"id":29896147523431,"type":"song","name":"Off the Wall","year":1980,"weight":17},{"id":29041711471818,"type":"song","name":"Black or White","year":1992,"weight":14},{"id":269627667806704,"type":"song","name":"Man in the Mirror","year":1988,"weight":13},{"id":168138684657987,"type":"album","name":"Dangerous","year":1991,